WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.215 --> 00:00:01.840
- [Woman] (speaking in foreign language)

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.240
- [Narrator] From airshow

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.830
to test flights in extreme cold weather

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.570
China state-owned aircraft
manufacturer Comac

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.060
has been ramping up the development

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:14.220
of its C919 passenger jet to
compete with Boeing and Airbus.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.910
- C919 is an important part of China's

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.120
national development strategy

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.230
- [Narrator] Though the project
is years behind schedule,

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.720
Beijing is moving ahead with big plans

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.300
at a time when the Coronavirus

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.740
has upended the aviation
industry around the world.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.730
Last December Comac began the process

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:34.400
of certifying the C919
for commercial operations.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.120
- The large economies have not recovered

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.310
as quickly as China

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:41.120
and therefore China's likely share

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.040
of future commercial aviation growth

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.030
is gonna be somewhat higher.

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:48.620
- [Narrator] Eventually the
government hopes the C919

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.860
will become the main carrier
in the world's biggest

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:53.933
commercial aviation
market, but can it succeed?

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.880
Chinese President Xi Jinping
has had an aviation dream

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.180
since he took office in 2012,

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.279
to build the country's first
commercial civilian airliner.

00:01:03.279 --> 00:01:06.612
- (in foreign language)

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:15.600
- [Narrator] For the past two decades,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.220
Airbus and Boeing have benefited

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.530
from China's fast-growing
commercial aviation market.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:23.730
Airbus built an assembly
plant in China in 2008.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.500
And before the pandemic, a quarter

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.950
of all Boeing planes that
came off the assembly line

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.320
went to China,

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.270
and the demand isn't
going away anytime soon.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.130
According to Boeing's
latest market outlook

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.820
from this past October,
it expects China to buy

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.510
more than 8,400 new airplanes
over the next 20 years

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.160
with the market valued at a total

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.690
of more than $1.7 trillion.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:47.120
- Is that very good economic reason

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.900
for China to want to
build its own aircraft.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:54.160
And that is so that it
can fill that market

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.500
and save a huge amount of it.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.340
- [Narrator] Timothy Heath
is a defense researcher

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.150
who's been studying China's
national aviation strategy

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:02.920
for more than 15 years.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:05.500
- [Timothy] The problem
is that due to it's

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.090
lack of experience, there's
a very steep learning curve.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.510
- [Narrator] For instance,
compared to Boeing's

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:12.770
more than 100 years of experience,

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:16.750
China started exploring
commercial aviation in the 1970s.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.210
So to catch up the Chinese
government has been focused

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:22.710
on Comac, which was only
established in 2008,

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.240
according to the US think tank

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.780
The Center for Strategic
and International Studies

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.840
since Comac's early days it has received

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.190
somewhere between $49 and $72
billion in government aid,

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:36.320
far more than the $22 billion
that Airbus has received

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.540
from European governments,

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.140
according to the World Trade Organization.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.670
Heath says while support from Beijing

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.910
has helped build successful
homegrown companies

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:47.290
and industries, including 5G
and artificial intelligence.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:50.470
It'll take more than money
to help the C919 take off.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:53.950
- The difference is that
civilian airliner manufacturers

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:56.810
is an order of magnitude more difficult

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.790
then a cell phone technology

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:01.230
and handheld consumer electronics.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.270
- [Narrator] That's because
building a commercial aircraft

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:05.680
requires hundreds of
thousands of components.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:06.840
- Their individual components,

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.730
which are ridiculously difficult to make

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.220
because you have to make them perfectly.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.090
And they have to work

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:16.760
at 35,000 feet in the
air for hour upon hour,

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.560
land, gas up, and do it
again with no problems.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.510
- Scott Kennedy is a senior advisor

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:25.400
at the Center for Strategic
and International Studies.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.490
The non-profit policy research
organization receives part

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:30.090
of its funding from some governments

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.310
and corporations including Boeing.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.080
Kennedy has been analyzing
China's industrial policy

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.020
for more than 25 years.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.260
- Most of the parts that the Chinese make

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.030
are in the interior or for elements

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:44.540
of the body or the doors.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.650
So the Chinese components
are relevant to the plane

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:51.180
but they're not central to
the plane's ability to fly.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.480
- [Narrator] The more
complex parts are imported.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.580
- [Scott] China depends almost
entirely on the US and Europe

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:01.520
for the components that go
into the plane from the engine,

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.700
to the avionics, to the materials,

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:08.020
to most of what's inside the plane, even.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.570
- [Narrator] According
to Kennedy's analysis

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:12.330
only 14 key suppliers are from China

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:15.370
and half of them are joint
ventures with foreign companies.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.600
And these joint ventures
are one important part

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.060
of Comac's plans to
advance technologically.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:23.260
- The Chinese have actually
required a support suppliers

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.560
to transfer technology in many cases.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.310
That means the Chinese
are absorbing technology

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:33.100
and they're learning how to
make some of the components.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:33.933
- [Narrator] But for years,

00:04:33.933 --> 00:04:36.880
Western manufacturers have
acted to protect their IP

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.130
by only supplying old technology.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:40.510
- It's already an obsolete plane

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.580
cause you've been using the oldest

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.400
most out of date technology

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.510
because the companies don't
want to share and give away

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.220
their most cutting edge,
valuable technologies.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.700
- [Narrator] Still the
Trump administration

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.580
kept an eye on joint ventures,

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.790
concerned that forced technology transfers

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.670
could allow China to break into
the global jet engine market

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:59.880
and undermined US businesses.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:03.480
- Then a world of heightened
diplomatic tensions

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:07.150
that are growing more severe by the day.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:11.610
One has to question whether
those diplomatic tensions

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:16.610
could eventually bring a
project like the C919 to a halt.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:18.670
- [Narrator] For
instance, in early January

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:21.700
the Trump administration added
Comac to a list of companies

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:24.000
it says support China's military.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.810
This blacklist could ban Americans

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:28.210
from supplying the plane manufacturer.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:31.230
Comac didn't respond to
a request for comment.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.420
It's uncertain how political
tensions will change

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:35.270
during the Biden administration.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.150
But Kennedy says the success
of Comac will take longer

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.740
than one presidential term.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:42.067
- Despite all of the state support

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:44.950
and the history of China overcoming

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:46.790
previous technological hurdles.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:50.020
I still think that we're no closer

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:53.740
then a decade away from Comac
being a serious competitor

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.920
to Boeing or Airbus.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:58.610
- [Narrator] Until then
China will need to rely

00:05:58.610 --> 00:05:59.660
on their jets.

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:02.220
But when the C919 is ready it potentially

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.750
has a guaranteed market at home

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.290
since Beijing could order
it's state-owned airlines

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.630
to buy the plane in large numbers.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.690
According to Kennedy's
analysis, Comac already had more

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:14.420
than 1,000 orders by the end of 2020.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:18.920
- These orders have been on
the books for a long time

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:22.140
but those numbers on
orders are really smoke

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:24.740
and mirrors until they really can prove

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:28.453
that they can deliver and service
planes on a regular basis.

